          %h1#theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            \-theory
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#universal_characterization"} Universal characterization
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToKKTheory"} Relation to KK-theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_shape_theory"} Relation to shape theory
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              \-Theory
            is the name of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            are homotopy classes of slightly generalized
            = succeed "-homomorphisms," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C*
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+C%2A-homomorphisms"} asymptotic C*-homomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            and are also called the
            %em E-groups
            of their arguments. Since under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            may be thought of as exhibiting
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+stable+homotopy+theory"} noncommutative stable homotopy theory
          %p
            This construction may be understood as the universal improvement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excision"} excision
            (
            %a{:href => "#Higson90"}> Higson 90
            ). Accordingly, the
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            (regarding, in view of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            on “noncommutative topological spaces”) one may understand this as dealing with “locally badly behaved space” such as certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            (
            %a{:href => "ConnesHigson90"}> Connes-Higson 90
            ) in a way that resembles a noncommutative version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+theory"} shape theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dadarlat94"}> Dādārlat 94
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p First some notation and terminology.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma A \coloneqq C_0((0,1),A)
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
            %em suspension
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A,B]
            for the set of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+C%2A-homomorphisms"} asymptotic C*-homomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                there is a natural
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition+operation"} composition operation
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A,B] \times [B,C] \to [A,C]
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A,\Sigma B]
                is naturally an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          %p
            Finally, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K} \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            for the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+operators"} compact operators
            on an infinite-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C^\ast Alg
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+C%2A-algebras"} tensor product of C*-algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝒦
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes \mathcal{K}
            is also called the
            %em stabilization
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              %strong E-group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ab
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E(A,B) \coloneqq [(\Sigma A )\otimes \mathcal{K}, (\Sigma B) \otimes \mathcal{K}]
                    \\in Ab
                    \\,.
            %p
              Under the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              operation this yields an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(-,-)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#universal_characterization Universal characterization
          %p
            E-theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal
            localization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to E
            which is homotopy-invariant, stable and preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequences"} exact sequences
            in the middle.
          %p (…)
          %h3#RelationToKKTheory Relation to KK-theory
          %p
            Because KK-theory is the universal
            %em split exact
            (stable and homotopy-invariant) localization of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} split exact sequence
            is in particular exact, there is a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KK \to E
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            to that of
            = succeed "-theory." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+C%2A-algebras"} nuclear C*-algebras
            this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Higson90"} Higson 90
          %p
            If in the definition of E-theory by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+C%2A-homomorphisms"} asymptotic C*-homomorphisms
            one restricts to those which take values in contractive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+positive+maps"} completely positive maps
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Introduction"} Introduction, p. 34
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KK
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK \to E
            is then just the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          %p
            It follows that the Kasparov product in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            is equivalently given by the composition of the corresponding completely positive
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+C%2A-homomorphisms"} asymptotic C*-homomorphisms
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-bootstrap+category"} KK-bootstrap category
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th geometric context
                  %th
                    universal additive
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivariant+cohomology+theory"} bivariant
