                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} …
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The idea of E-theory was introduced in
          %ul#ConnesHigson90
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Higson"} Nigel Higson
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Déformations, morphismes asymptotiques et
                  = succeed "-th\u00E9orie" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %strong 311
              (1990), no. 2, 101–106,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1065438"} MR91m:46114
              %a{:href => "ftp://ftp.bnf.fr/578/N5781521_PDF_107_112DM.pdf"} pdf
          %ul#Higson90
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Higson"}> Nigel Higson
              ,
              %em Categories of fractions and excision in KK-theory
              J. Pure Appl. Algebra, 65(2):119–138, (1990) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.psu.edu/higson/math/Papers_files/Higson%20-%201990%20-%20Categories%20of%20fractions%20and%20excision%20in%20KK-theory.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Reviews and surveys include
          %ul#Introduction
            %li
              %em> Introduction to KK-theory and E-theory
              , Lecture notes (Lisbon 2009) (
              %a{:href => "http://oaa.ist.utl.pt/files/cursos/courseD_Lecture4_KK_and_E1.pdf"}> pdf slides
              )
          %p A standard textbook account is in section 25 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Blackadar"}> Bruce Blackadar
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-Theory+for+Operator+Algebras"} K-Theory for Operator Algebras
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            aspects are further discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Martin Grensing,
                %em Noncommutative stable homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.4751"}> arXiv:1302.4751
                )
            %li
              %p
                Rasmus Bentmann,
                %em Homotopy-theoretic E-theory and n-order
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.6924"}> arXiv:1302.6924
                )
          %p See also
          %ul#Mahanta
            %li
              %p
                web page of a project
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ku.dk/~jg/papers/etheory.html"} Noncommutative topology - homotopy functors and E-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snigdhayan+Mahanta"}> Snigdhayan Mahanta
                ,
                %em
                  Higher nonunital Quillen
                  = succeed "-theory," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K'
                  = succeed "-duality" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕋
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/snigdhayan.mahanta/papers/KQ.pdf"} pdf
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://faculty.tcu.edu/epark/papers/ETheory_JFA.pdf"} pdf
